 :description
 "How the parts of the Smile system were named between July and August 2026, grove, plant, stem, rhizome, surfacing and phenotype, then names that say what each part literally does, then figurations from Deleuze and Guattari, and the names THE MAP keeps, with every source.",
 :keywords
 "naming a software system, biomimicry names, rhizome, Deleuze and Guattari, figuration, lens, Smile prompt language, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "A name in Smile is a figuration the system grows into. If the metaphor is truly aligned, the meaning of the system grows into the structure the name defines.",
 :paras
 ["These names have no heading of their own in THE MAP. They are the search for what to call the parts of the system, and THE MAP keeps many of the names it found, among them render, ring, card, lens, tier and the Field. Lens is followed in [[t:lens]]."
 "On 26 July 2026 names from living things came into the work on my PC. “I love grove, plant, stem, composition as rhizome I think is great.”, “Also I love surfacing, and phenotype is great.”, “composing can be called grow.”, and “this also means that the inference is a blossoming”. Their purpose was the ontology, “It is the ontological aspect which is essential for organization and tonnes of other things in the future.”[[m:2026-07-26]]"
 "Three days later I asked for names that say what each part literally is, and gave the reason for any name. “none of the biological naming evident, just describe what it literally does and what it literally is on the system”, and “if it's true metaphoric alignment, where we define a structure and the meaning of the system grows into it, then that's what matters.”[[m:2026-07-29]] On 1 August I asked for names “influenced by D&G”.[[m:2026-08-01]] On 8 August, “we are choosing complicated biomimicry ideas as a way of building a stronger energetic blueprint for our ideas to move through”, and “figurations are what you grow into.”[[m:2026-08-08]] On 11 August, “use mirrored as the term not reversed”.[[m:2026-08-11]] On 12 August, “you can put it all in terms of the things we are using, eg ontologies, lenses, modules, compositions.”[[m:2026-08-12]]"
 "On 30 August the search went deeper into biology and philosophy. “i want a biomimicy rhizome/tuber/nonlinear friendly figuration metaphor for it to grow into”, and “you need to examine first what they mean in a bio context, then a tech context, then propose something where the meanings are the same metaphorical;ly across both”.[[m:2026-08-30]]"
 "So the names moved from grove and plant in July 2026, to literal descriptions, to figurations whose meaning matches in biology and in the system, across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes from {{first}} to {{last}}."],
